    "updated_at": "2026-10-17T11:21:55Z",
    "body": "Reproduced on langchain-core 1.6.12 with the snippet above: the truncated args land in tool_calls as {'type': 'hea'} and invalid_tool_calls stays empty, so a cut-off stream produces a valid-looking tool call with half its input.\n\nThe fix direction looks like what you describe: the final aggregation path (generate_from_stream / the last chunk) should parse args strictly and route failures to invalid_tool_calls with the raw string preserved, keeping lenient parsing only for in-flight chunks.\n\nI'd like to work on this - could you assign it to me?",
